WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:02.708
(jazzy music)

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.937
- I don't know what I was thinking.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:17.567
So I'm a big fan of Casey Neistat,

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:20.806
and I've been following his vlog

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:23.056
since 2015 when it started.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.517
And at that time in my life, I thought it was too late

00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:28.684
to pursue any kind of creative career.

00:00:28.702 --> 00:00:30.382
But after watching him and listening to his story,

00:00:30.382 --> 00:00:31.723
I realized that it wasn't too late.

00:00:31.723 --> 00:00:34.123
I spent all my time online learning how to make videos,

00:00:34.123 --> 00:00:36.174
and it eventually led me here to New York City.

00:00:36.174 --> 00:00:37.414
I'm really curious what a day in the life

00:00:37.414 --> 00:00:38.723
of Casey Neistat looks like,

00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:40.873
so I'm gonna try to run like Casey,

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.222
every day, for the next five days.

00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:44.894
Before I can run like Casey,

00:00:44.894 --> 00:00:47.174
I need to figure out how far he actually runs.

00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:48.334
- About 10 miles per day.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.062
We watched over 200 of the original vlogs

00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:53.414
and he mentions running in 37 of them,

00:00:53.414 --> 00:00:56.497
and out of those 37 he ran 369 miles,

00:00:56.745 --> 00:01:00.824
and if you divide that up, it's about 10 miles per day.

00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:02.923
- About to take the first couple steps on day one here.

00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:05.256
(rap music)

00:01:08.424 --> 00:01:10.625
Calves are really starting to tighten up.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:12.883
Yeah, this is tough, this is really tough.

00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:14.654
Alright seven miles in,

00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:17.465
kinda reaching that limit, three more.

00:01:17.465 --> 00:01:19.385
Just passed the eight mile mark, everything

00:01:19.385 --> 00:01:21.774
in my body's telling me to stop, two more to go.

00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:22.941
10 miles done.

00:01:23.225 --> 00:01:24.614
Oh my god, I'm tired.

00:01:24.614 --> 00:01:26.523
I can already feel my legs starting to like,

00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:29.372
we will see how I feel in the morning.

00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:30.622
So far so good.

00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:34.933
Alright so it's day two and I am already so impressed

00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:38.533
with Casey, I don't know how he does this every single day.

00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:42.533
Alright one mile done, today feels rough so far.

00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:46.808
Casey definitely runs down this pier.

00:01:47.484 --> 00:01:48.901
Seven more to go.

00:01:49.203 --> 00:01:52.786
Look at that, this is such a good spot too.

00:01:53.395 --> 00:01:55.978
(upbeat music)

00:02:02.617 --> 00:02:04.726
I don't know how you do this everyday.

00:02:04.726 --> 00:02:07.726
Put your phone down, run, come back.

00:02:08.825 --> 00:02:11.275
I mean that really adds some distance after a while.

00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:13.115
I wasted a lot of time filming stuff.

00:02:13.115 --> 00:02:15.217
I have to run the next five miles in under an hour

00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:16.894
to get back to work in time for a shoot,

00:02:16.894 --> 00:02:18.897
so I gotta just keep going.

00:02:18.897 --> 00:02:21.183
I'll check back in at the end.

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:23.016
Another 10 miles done.

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:26.608
The last two were a real, real struggle.

00:02:27.693 --> 00:02:29.526
Okay, on to day three.

00:02:30.046 --> 00:02:30.879
My hood--

00:02:32.046 --> 00:02:34.817
Alright, to be totally honest, this part gets boring,

00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:37.147
I'm running, I'm tired, I'm sore, alright we get it,

00:02:37.147 --> 00:02:39.246
so let's just jump ahead to day four,

00:02:39.246 --> 00:02:43.014
but the end of day four, and we'll go from there.

00:02:43.014 --> 00:02:45.094
That was the worst run yet.

00:02:45.094 --> 00:02:49.785
I mean, everything is just (bleep) soaked.

00:02:49.785 --> 00:02:51.275
So if you're a fan of the old vlogs,

00:02:51.275 --> 00:02:53.385
you know that Casey would run in the city

00:02:53.385 --> 00:02:56.086
quite a bit but he'd also run somewhere else.

00:02:56.086 --> 00:03:00.625
So if I'm gonna run like Casey, I gotta really go for it.

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:03.042
(rock music)

00:03:14.566 --> 00:03:16.645
Alright, a few hours later, I am out of the city

00:03:16.645 --> 00:03:17.665
in New London, Connecticut

00:03:17.665 --> 00:03:21.082
for my final day of running, let's do it.

00:03:24.115 --> 00:03:25.755
Alright, beach was super fun,

00:03:25.755 --> 00:03:28.338
I'm gonna head to the town now.

00:03:33.105 --> 00:03:36.188
I'm so close to finishing, oh my god.

00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:40.786
The week's really catching up to me today.

00:03:41.006 --> 00:03:42.089
Almost there.

00:03:42.372 --> 00:03:45.883
I feel a lot slower running here, 'cause you can see so far.

00:03:45.883 --> 00:03:48.485
In the city I'm just flying past people

00:03:48.485 --> 00:03:50.193
and buildings, it feels so quick.

00:03:50.193 --> 00:03:52.360
I'm not very fast I guess.

00:03:54.145 --> 00:03:55.812
Oh my god, I did it.

00:03:57.254 --> 00:03:59.054
(bleep)

00:03:59.054 --> 00:04:01.155
That was stupid, I don't wanna ever do this again.

00:04:01.155 --> 00:04:04.655
10 miles, every day for five days is done.

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:06.745
I need something to eat.

00:04:08.995 --> 00:04:10.075
Well it's done.

00:04:10.075 --> 00:04:12.445
I ran 10 miles a day for five days.

00:04:12.445 --> 00:04:14.865
I am exhausted, my whole body is so sore.

00:04:14.865 --> 00:04:17.355
I respect the guy even more, to run 10 miles,

00:04:17.355 --> 00:04:19.705
and film it, and vlog your life.

00:04:19.705 --> 00:04:21.945
I don't know how he balances it all, I really don't.

00:04:21.945 --> 00:04:23.612
I gotta work harder.

00:04:29.475 --> 00:04:31.808
Ah, (bleep)

